     "explanation": "Make Time is a menu, not a meal. The authors expect you to keep roughly ten tactics, and they advise starting minimally — about one tactic per step — so the system is light enough to survive a hard week. You then grow it through the Reflect loop, letting each addition earn its place with evidence. Installing everything at once collapses, and copying the authors' personal set ignores that the right tactics are the ones that fit your life.",
